    "title": "Wyoming soccer draws with New Mexico | University of Wyoming | wyomingnews.com",
    "text": "Sixty-five seconds became the difference between a win and a draw for University of Wyoming soccer.\nCelina Frenz’s equalizer at 88 minutes, 55 seconds helped New Mexico tie the Cowgirls, 1-1, on Thursday at the Indoor Practice Facility in Laramie.\nIt marked the Cowgirls’ (10-3-1 overall, 3-1-1 Mountain West) first draw of the season and snapped a two-match winning streak.\nEach squad fired 13 shots, though the Lobos outshot UW, 8-6, with shots on goal.\nWyoming’s Erin Dahl opened the scoring in the 15th minute.\nThe Cowgirls host Texas-El Paso at 1 p.m. Sunday.",
    "summary": "Sixty-five seconds became the difference between a win and a draw for University of Wyoming soccer. Celina Frenz’s equalizer at 88 minutes, 55 seconds helped New Mexico tie the Cowgirls, 1-1, on Thursday at the Indoor Practice Facility in Laramie. It marked the Cowgirls’ (10-3-1 overall, 3-1-1 Mountain West) first draw of the season and snapped a two-match winning streak. Wyoming’s Erin Dahl opened the scoring in the 15th minute. The Cowgirls host Texas-El Paso at 1 p.m. Sunday.",
